# Create Template

## File Purpose and Relationship

This manual Project Rule defines the specific standards, procedures, and tool call sequences for handling the `create-template` message-command in the documentation workflow of the PolygonExpress project. It should be consulted when:

- Creating standardized documentation templates
- Establishing structure for new component documentation
- Initializing API endpoint documentation
- Developing architecture and workflow documentation templates
- Ensuring consistent documentation format across the project

This file is designed to be used as a project-rule-parameter with the `create-template` message-command:
```
create-template: {doc-type} @manual/documentation/create-template.mdc
```

This file complements:
- **documentation-workflow.mdc**: Core documentation workflow processes
- **create-official-documentation.mdc**: Process for creating documentation from templates
- **verify-official-documentation.mdc**: Process for verifying documentation accuracy

When information appears to conflict, this file takes precedence for documentation template creation standards.

## 1. Template Creation Approach

The documentation template creation process follows a type-specific approach designed to maximize completeness, consistency, and implementation accuracy:

### Template Creation Philosophy

1. **Type-Specific Structure**: Tailor template structure to documentation type
2. **Comprehensive Sections**: Include all required sections based on documentation standards
3. **Guided Content**: Provide clear guidance for completing each section
4. **Implementation-First**: Structure templates to encourage verification against actual code
5. **Cross-Reference Support**: Build in proper linking to related documentation

## 2. Required Tool Call Sequence

You MUST follow this specific tool call sequence when creating documentation templates:

### Step 1: Determine Template Type

```
list_dir("official-documentation")
```

Check existing documentation structure to identify appropriate domain and relationships.

### Step 2: Create Template Based on Document Type

For Component Documentation:
```
edit_file("official-documentation/[domain]/[component-name].md",
          "Create standardized component documentation template",
          "# [Component Name]\n\n## Purpose\n\n[Brief description of the component's role in the system.]\n\n## Component Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    Component[Component Name] --> SubComponent1[Sub-Component 1]\n    Component --> SubComponent2[Sub-Component 2]\n```\n\n[Brief explanation of the architectural relationships.]\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n### Key Functions/Methods\n\n| Function | Purpose | Parameters | Return Value |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `functionName` | [Description] | `param1`: type - description | Return type - description |\n\n### Interfaces/Types\n\n```typescript\ninterface ComponentProps {\n  // Interface definition\n}\n```\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n### Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\n// Example code showing basic usage\n```\n\n### Advanced Usage\n\n```typescript\n// Example code showing advanced usage\n```\n\n## Related Components\n\n- [Component 1](../path/to/component1.md) - Relationship description\n- [Component 2](../path/to/component2.md) - Relationship description\n\n## Last Verified\n\n[YYYY-MM-DD] - Verified against commit [hash] by [verifier]")
```

For API Documentation:
```
edit_file("official-documentation/[domain]/[api-name].md",
          "Create standardized API documentation template",
          "# [API Name]\n\n## Purpose\n\n[Brief description of the API's purpose and role in the system.]\n\n## API Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    Client->>+Server: API Request\n    Server-->>-Client: API Response\n```\n\n[Brief explanation of the API flow and architecture.]\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### `[HTTP Method] /api/[endpoint-path]`\n\n**Purpose**: [Description of what this endpoint does]\n\n#### Request\n\n**Headers**:\n\n| Header | Required | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Authorization` | Yes/No | [Description] |\n\n**Parameters**:\n\n| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `paramName` | string | Yes/No | [Description] |\n\n**Body**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"property\": \"value\"\n}\n```\n\n#### Response\n\n**Status Codes**:\n\n| Status | Description |\n|---|---|\n| 200 | [Success description] |\n| 400 | [Error description] |\n\n**Response Body**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"property\": \"value\"\n}\n```\n\n## Data Models\n\n### `[ModelName]`\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `property` | string | [Description] |\n\n## Error Handling\n\n| Error Code | Meaning | Resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ERROR_CODE` | [Description] | [How to resolve] |\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n### Basic Request\n\n```typescript\n// Example code showing basic API usage\n```\n\n## Related APIs\n\n- [API 1](../path/to/api1.md) - Relationship description\n- [API 2](../path/to/api2.md) - Relationship description\n\n## Last Verified\n\n[YYYY-MM-DD] - Verified against commit [hash] by [verifier]")
